Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm6115-pro1x: the headset jack's MBHC thresholds

The sound card registers the WCD9370's jack (sm8250.c, through
qcom_snd_wcd_jack_setup on the TX_CODEC_DMA_TX_3 link: the "Headset
Jack" input device, the "Headphone Jack" and "Mic Jack" controls) and
wcd937x starts its MBHC, but the codec node had no MBHC properties.
wcd_dt_parse_mbhc_data() then logs "missing
qcom,mbhc-buttons-vthreshold-microvolt" and sets every button threshold
to 500000, which wcd937x_mbhc_program_btn_thr() takes as millivolts:
(500000 * 2 / 25) & 0x3f is 0, so all eight thresholds were 0 mV and
the headset buttons could not be told apart.

The thresholds are the Pro1X vendor kernel's (bengal.c,
def_wcd_mbhc_cal: 75, 150, 237 mV, then 500 mV), the same as every
upstream WCD93xx board. The headset and headphone thresholds equal the
driver's defaults (1.7 V, 50 mV) and are given as the other boards do.
The vendor device tree has qcom,msm-mbhc-hphl-swh and gnd-swh = 1
(normally open), which is the binding's default (no
*-normally-closed), and no US/Euro switch GPIO.

The jack's DAPM pins stay unrouted on purpose: the AW87339s sit behind
the WCD9370's HPH outputs, so a "Headphone Jack" widget behind
HPHL/HPHR would end the codec outputs' endpoint status and switch the
loudspeaker path with the jack. User space switches by the controls
(UCM JackControl).

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115-fxtec-pro1x.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115-fxtec-pro1x.dts
index 703dfd9731..91755b757a 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115-fxtec-pro1x.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115-fxtec-pro1x.dts
@@ -407,6 +407,20 @@ wcd9370: audio-codec {
 		qcom,micbias3-microvolt = <1800000>;
 		qcom,micbias4-microvolt = <1800000>;
 
+		/*
+		 * The headset jack (MBHC). The button thresholds are the vendor
+		 * kernel's (bengal.c, def_wcd_mbhc_cal): without them the driver
+		 * takes 500000 for each, in millivolts, which the threshold
+		 * registers (6 bits of mV * 2 / 25) truncate to 0. Headset and
+		 * headphone thresholds as the driver's defaults. The L-detect and
+		 * ground switches are normally open (vendor qcom,msm-mbhc-hphl-swh
+		 * and gnd-swh = 1), the binding's default; no US/Euro switch.
+		 */
+		qcom,mbhc-buttons-vthreshold-microvolt = <75000 150000 237000 500000
+							  500000 500000 500000 500000>;
+		qcom,mbhc-headset-vthreshold-microvolt = <1700000>;
+		qcom,mbhc-headphone-vthreshold-microvolt = <50000>;
+
 		qcom,rx-device = <&wcd937x_rx>;
 		qcom,tx-device = <&wcd937x_tx>;
 
